          ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $G,$ given by\n\n$$\nG=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2}$ on $G?$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $-5$ times the second row to the third row. \n\nApplying this row operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-5)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0+(-5)(0) & 5+(-5)(1) & 6+(-5)(2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
